{title: When Your Majesty Comes}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
The beauty of a mountain stream
Surrounded with a blanket of green
Will pale in its beauty
When Your majesty comes.

Verse 2
The stars up in the heavens
That shine for all the world to see
Will fail in their brilliance
When Your majesty comes.

chorus
And all creation
Is yearning for Your return.
A day of celebration
When Your majesty comes!
When Your majesty comes!!
When Your majesty comes!!!

verse 2
In that day we will understand
How everything has worked for the good
Your glory revealed
When Your majesty comes.

Verse 3
For though we see the shadows
The veil of time will be removed
To know You completely
When Your majesty comes.

Verse 4
[repeat chorus]

bridge
Let the trumpet sound...
The heavens open wide...
The day that we've been longing for:
Our sovereign Lord
Descending from the sky!

Verse 5
[repeat chorus -- on last line, slow and sustain]
